        <body>
            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0812" n="706" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg706"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Carter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 354.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Newfoundland fishery
                    question, I quote for your information the substance of a telegram, dated the
                    6th instant, from Fisheries Agent Alexander:</p>
                <p>“Fishermen fuify aware importance complying with the requirements of modus
                    vivendi. No further trouble expected on account fishing Sunday.”</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d582-a1.xml" xpointer="d582-a1"/>
